# Low-level: generic dispatcher to ONE of core::WooDrive's individual
# per-register gain/limit setters (setPositionPGain(), setVelocityCcwMax(),
# etc.) -- one field, one serial round-trip, exactly like calling that
# setter directly. `field` must be one of the names below (snake_case);
# unknown names are rejected without touching the serial port.
#
# Gain fields (see command_utils.hpp isKnownGainLimitField() for the
# authoritative list):
#   gain_mode, position_gain_scale, velocity_gain_scale, current_gain_scale,
#   position_p_gain, velocity_p_gain, velocity_i_gain, current_p_gain, current_i_gain
# Limit fields:
#   position_ccw_max, position_cw_max, velocity_ccw_max, velocity_cw_max,
#   iq_current_ccw_max, iq_current_cw_max, id_current_max, iq_current_limit,
#   bus_voltage_max_limit, bus_voltage_min_limit, temperature_max_limit
#
# `value` is a plain double regardless of the field's wire type (uint8/
# uint32/float) -- the node casts it to whatever the target register needs.
# No range clamping is applied; this is a tuning interface, use with care
# (see ~/motion_command's docs on why raw setters aren't validated for
# "sane" values -- that judgment call is left to the caller).

string field
float64 value
---
bool success
string message
